#!/usr/bin/python3
"""glaeda-seed-archive: keep the fleet's seed archive (cmux-lawrence) filled from the trusted seeder.

    glaeda-seed-archive                    plan: the seeds the seeder keeps that the archive lacks
    glaeda-seed-archive --apply            fetch them newest first, then prune (the LaunchDaemon, every 15 s)
    glaeda-seed-archive install [--apply]  write and load that LaunchDaemon (run on the archive host)
    glaeda-seed-archive uninstall [--apply]  boot out and remove the daemon and any old LaunchAgent

cmuxterm-hq#821. The owned minis' j14 DerivedData seeds are built by one trusted-only seeder (cmux15), which
keeps only its recent ones on a 460 GB disk. The archive keeps them all, up to BUDGET, on cmux-lawrence's
X10 Pro SSD, and the PR minis read seeds from it (glaeda-seed-lan install --seeder cmux-lawrence --role archive,
then glaeda-seed-serve --role archive answers glaeda-seed-prefetch). A seed lands here within about a minute of
the seeder keeping it, over the LAN, instead of every mini downloading it from R2.

The job is a system LaunchDaemon (/Library/LaunchDaemons, UserName this user, `launchctl bootstrap system`), not a
LaunchAgent: the archive host serves the fleet headless, and an agent stops when its login session ends (cmux-lawrence
rebooted 2026-11-20 ~09:00Z and every agent of its user stopped with the session). `install --apply` needs root for the plist and launchctl: `sudo -n` (SUDO_PREFIX, overridable by
GLAEDA_SEED_ARCHIVE_SUDO; none as root); without passwordless sudo it prints the root commands (run them with
`fleet-sudo HOST ...`) and exits 1, never falling back to an agent. It migrates: the old gui/UID agent is booted out
and its plist removed first. A daemon already loaded from hand under the same label is adopted, not duplicated.

The job asks every INTERVAL (15 s) seconds. It used to ask every 5 minutes, and a PR mini's prefetch
(also every 5 minutes) that came between the seeder keeping a seed and the archive's next run missed here and
fell back to R2 at about 3 MB/s beside a job (755 to 1163 s instead of 63 to 184 s over the LAN): 14 of the
68 misses on 2026-09-28 05:22-12:20Z were that wait. Asking costs one `seed-list-v1` round trip (a directory
listing on the seeder), and a run with nothing to fetch or prune writes nothing. Polling keeps the direction
as it was: the archive asks the trusted seeder, which never connects to the archive or reads from it.

Each seed is kept as ARCHIVE/<KEY>.tar.zst: exactly the zstd stream the seeder's glaeda-seed-serve sends (a
tar of one top-level directory named KEY), so serving it is a plain read. ARCHIVE is inside IMAGE, an APFS
sparse bundle on the (ExFAT) X10 Pro, mounted at MOUNT: macOS privacy (TCC) lets a launchd job running
/usr/bin/python3 write into an attached disk image but not onto the external volume itself (measured on
cmux-lawrence 2026-09-28, "Operation not permitted"; Lawrence's siso cache uses a sparse bundle on T5 EVO the
same way). Each run attaches the image if it is not mounted; `install --apply`, run over SSH, creates it. The
archive is a client of the seeder like any mini (glaeda-seed-lan install --seeder cmux15 ... cmux-lawrence
writes SEED_LAN_CONFIG); it asks `seed-list-v1` for the seeder's kept seeds and `seed-v1 zstd KEY` for each
one it lacks. A stream is written to a dot-file beside the archive, checked (every entry under KEY/, the seed
manifest present, under LAN_MAX_BYTES of zstd), and only then renamed into place.

Trust: the bytes come only from the trusted seeder, whose serve refuses unless its runner receipt names a
trusted ref; this host runs no jobs (glaeda-seed-serve --role archive refuses on a host with a runner
receipt), and the minis' keys here are forced-command, read-only.

Prune: oldest mtime first (glaeda-seed-serve touches a seed it serves) while the archive holds more than
BUDGET bytes or HOST_VOLUME has less than MIN_FREE free (the disk is Lawrence's). The newest KEEP_NEWEST and
anything touched in the last GRACE seconds stay.

Local Network Privacy: the job's program is /bin/sh (an Apple platform binary that stays the job's
process) running /usr/bin/python3, whose children are /usr/bin/ssh and Homebrew zstd (which only reads a
pipe), so the LAN connection is allowed. On macOS 27 a /usr/bin/python3 program alone is refused: it runs
Xcode's python3 (glaeda-mini-setup LAN_PARENT).
Prints one JSON line, also appended to LOG.

Disk errors: every run also writes DISK_ERRORS_NAME under STATE's parent (~/.local/state/glaeda/disk-errors/
seed-archive.json, schema glaeda-disk-errors/v1): how many archive entries read an OSError this run (EIO from a failing
drive under the image), how many sit quarantined as .corrupt-*, and a few examples. A dying drive then reads as a
disk-error row where NOW reads this service's health (leo-workspace tools/now_host_services.py, the registry's
`disk_errors`), not as a crash loop (cmux-lawrence 2026-11-27: 19 of 341 entries read EIO and a copy without the
per-entry guard restarted every 15 s; cmuxterm-hq docs/handbook/one-read-takes-down-the-pass.md).
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import fcntl
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import json
import os
import plistlib
import pwd
import shutil
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from pathlib import Path

SCRIPT_DIR = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
HOME = Path(os.path.expanduser("~"))
HOST_VOLUME = Path("/Volumes/X10 Pro")
IMAGE = HOST_VOLUME / "glaeda-seed-archive.sparsebundle"
IMAGE_SIZE = "1t"  # the most it can grow to; BUDGET keeps it below
MOUNT = Path("/Volumes/glaeda-seed-archive")
ARCHIVE = MOUNT / "seeds"  # glaeda-seed-serve ARCHIVE
# The first version kept the files directly on the X10 Pro, where launchd jobs cannot write; install moves them.
OLD_ARCHIVE = HOST_VOLUME / "glaeda-seed-archive"
HDIUTIL = "/usr/bin/hdiutil"
SUFFIX = ".tar.zst"
CORRUPT = ".corrupt-"  # quarantine()'s prefix for a seed whose entry read an OSError
DISK_ERRORS_SCHEMA = "glaeda-disk-errors/v1"
DISK_ERRORS_NAME = "seed-archive.json"  # in STATE.parent / "disk-errors"
DISK_ERRORS_EXAMPLES = 5
STATE = HOME / ".local/state/glaeda/seed-archive"
LOG = HOME / "Library/Logs/glaeda-seed-archive.jsonl"
LOG_BYTES = 4 << 20
BUDGET = 800 * 1024**3
MIN_FREE = 300 * 1024**3
KEEP_NEWEST = 4
GRACE = 600  # a seed touched this recently may be streaming to a mini
MAX_PER_RUN = 8  # ~25 s each at LAN speed; the next run takes the rest
LIST_TIMEOUT = 30
FETCH_TIMEOUT = 420  # the seeder may wait 60 s for a slot, then streams within its 180 s limit
STALE_INCOMING = 3600
LABEL = "com.teamleaderleo.glaeda.seed-archive"
DAEMON_DIR = Path(os.environ.get("GLAEDA_SEED_ARCHIVE_DAEMON_DIR", "/Library/LaunchDaemons"))
SUDO_PREFIX = os.environ.get("GLAEDA_SEED_ARCHIVE_SUDO", "/usr/bin/sudo -n").split()
LAUNCHCTL = "/bin/launchctl"
INTERVAL = 15  # seconds between runs; launchd never starts one while the last still runs


def prefetch_module():
    """glaeda-seed-prefetch, installed beside this script: its LAN client (config, ssh, header, zstd)."""
    loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("glaeda_seed_prefetch_for_archive",
                                                  os.fspath(SCRIPT_DIR / "glaeda-seed-prefetch"))
    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader(loader.name, loader)
    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)
    sys.modules[loader.name] = module  # dataclasses look their module up in sys.modules while it loads
    loader.exec_module(module)
    return module


pm = prefetch_module()


def archived(archive: Path, unreadable: dict[str, str] | None = None,
             aside: list[str] | None = None) -> dict[str, os.stat_result]:
    """KEY -> stat of every archived seed (regular files named <KEY>.tar.zst).

    A seed whose entry cannot be read (EIO from a bad disk image or volume) is left out and, when UNREADABLE is
    given, recorded there as KEY -> error: one bad seed must not crash the run (the daemon did, 2026-11-21).
    ASIDE, when given, gets the name of every seed quarantine() moved aside (.corrupt-*), read from the same listing.
    """
    found = {}
    try:
        entries = list(os.scandir(archive))
    except OSError as error:
        if unreadable is not None:
            unreadable[""] = f"listing {archive}: {error}"
        return found
    for entry in entries:
        key = entry.name[:-len(SUFFIX)]
        if aside is not None and entry.name.startswith(CORRUPT):
            aside.append(entry.name)
        if entry.name.endswith(SUFFIX) and pm.KEY_RE.fullmatch(key):
            try:
                if entry.is_file(follow_symlinks=False):
                    found[key] = entry.stat(follow_symlinks=False)
            except OSError as error:
                if unreadable is not None:
                    unreadable[key] = f"{type(error).__name__} errno {error.errno}: {error.strerror}"
    return found


def quarantine(archive: Path, unreadable: dict[str, str], apply: bool) -> list[dict]:
    """Move each unreadable seed aside to .corrupt-<name> (a dot-file the archive and the server never list), and
    report it. A rename that fails too (the entry is as bad as its data) leaves it, reported, and the seed is not
    fetched over it. Nothing else on the volume is written, and never a repair: a disk check is the host's job."""
    report = []
    for key, why in sorted(unreadable.items()):
        if not key:
            report.append({"error": why})
            continue
        name = key + SUFFIX
        item = {"key": key, "error": why, "quarantined": False}
        if apply:
            try:
                os.rename(archive / name, archive / f"{CORRUPT}{name}")
                item["quarantined"] = True
            except OSError as error:
                item["quarantine_error"] = f"errno {error.errno}: {error.strerror}"
        report.append(item)
    return report


def ask(config: dict, request: str) -> subprocess.Popen:
    """/usr/bin/ssh to the seeder with REQUEST; the caller reads the header then the stream."""
    return subprocess.Popen(pm.ssh_command(config, config["addresses"][0], request), stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL,
                            stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE)


def seeder_list(config: dict) -> tuple[list[tuple[str, int]], str]:
    """The seeder's kept seeds (key, mtime), newest first, or [] and why (glaeda-seed-prefetch's client)."""
    return pm.seed_list(config, config["addresses"][0], LIST_TIMEOUT)


def check(path: Path, key: str) -> str:
    """"" when PATH is a zstd tar of one directory KEY holding the seed manifest, else why not."""
    zstd = pm.zstd_tool()
    if not zstd:
        return "no zstd"
    unpack = subprocess.Popen([zstd, "-d", "-q", "-c", os.fspath(path)], stdout=subprocess.PIPE,
                              stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)
    try:
        listing = subprocess.run([pm.TAR, "-t", "-f", "-"], stdin=unpack.stdout, capture_output=True, timeout=600)
        unpacked = unpack.wait(timeout=60)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        unpack.kill()
        unpack.wait()
        return "check timed out"
    finally:
        unpack.stdout.close()
    if unpacked != 0 or listing.returncode != 0:
        return "not a readable zstd tar"
    names = [n.rstrip("/") for n in listing.stdout.decode(errors="replace").splitlines()]
    # Everything under KEY/ (bsdtar may add an AppleDouble ._KEY beside it), no absolute or .. paths.
    stray = [n for n in names if n.startswith("/") or ".." in n.split("/")
             or not (n in (key, "._" + key) or n.startswith(key + "/"))]
    if stray:
        return f"entry outside {key}: {stray[0][:80]}"
    if f"{key}/{pm.MANIFEST}" not in names:
        return "no seed manifest"
    return ""


def fetch(config: dict, key: str, archive: Path) -> dict:
    """Stream KEY from the seeder into the archive; the outcome."""
    started = time.monotonic()
    incoming = archive / f".{key}{SUFFIX}.incoming-{os.getpid()}"
    proc = ask(config, f"seed-v1 zstd {key}")
    compress = None
    try:
        header = pm.read_header(proc.stdout.fileno())
        words = header[len(pm.SERVE_HEADER):].decode(errors="replace").split()
        if not header.startswith(pm.SERVE_HEADER):
            proc.kill()
            return {"key": key, "outcome": "unreachable",
                    "detail": proc.stderr.read().decode(errors="replace").strip()[-160:]}
        if words[:1] != ["hit"]:
            proc.kill()
            return {"key": key, "outcome": (words[:1] or ["empty"])[0]}  # miss, busy, refused
        if len(words) != 3 or words[1] != key or words[2] not in ("zstd", "tar"):
            proc.kill()
            return {"key": key, "outcome": "bad-answer", "detail": " ".join(words)[:120]}
        with open(incoming, "wb") as out:
            source = proc.stdout
            if words[2] == "tar":  # a seeder without zstd: compress here
                if not pm.zstd_tool():
                    proc.kill()
                    return {"key": key, "outcome": "no-zstd"}
                compress = subprocess.Popen([pm.zstd_tool(), "-1", "-T0", "-q", "-c"], stdin=proc.stdout,
                                            stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL)
                proc.stdout.close()
                source = compress.stdout
            total, deadline = 0, time.monotonic() + FETCH_TIMEOUT
            while chunk := source.read(1 << 20):
                total += len(chunk)
                if total > pm.LAN_MAX_BYTES or time.monotonic() > deadline:
                    proc.kill()
                    return {"key": key, "outcome": "too-big-or-slow", "bytes": total}
                out.write(chunk)
            out.flush()
            os.fsync(out.fileno())
        try:
            failed = proc.wait(timeout=60) != 0 or (compress and compress.wait(timeout=60) != 0)
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            failed = True
        if failed:
            return {"key": key, "outcome": "stream-failed", "bytes": total}
        streamed = time.monotonic() - started
        if why := check(incoming, key):
            return {"key": key, "outcome": "rejected", "detail": why, "bytes": total}
        os.rename(incoming, archive / (key + SUFFIX))
        return {"key": key, "outcome": "fetched", "bytes": total, "seconds": round(streamed, 1),
                "checked_seconds": round(time.monotonic() - started - streamed, 1)}
    finally:
        for p in (proc, compress):
            if p and p.poll() is None:
                p.kill()
                p.wait()
            for pipe in (p.stdout, p.stderr) if p else ():
                if pipe:
                    pipe.close()
        try:
            incoming.unlink()
        except OSError:
            pass


def prune(archive: Path, budget: int, min_free: int, apply: bool, spare: set[str] = frozenset()) -> list[dict]:
    """Delete the oldest archived seeds while over BUDGET or under MIN_FREE; what was (or would be) deleted.

    SPARE (the seeds the seeder still keeps) stay: deleting one would only fetch it again next run.
    """
    now = time.time()
    for stale in archive.glob(".*.incoming-*"):
        try:
            if now - stale.stat().st_mtime > STALE_INCOMING and apply:
                stale.unlink()
        except OSError:
            pass
    seeds = sorted(archived(archive).items(), key=lambda item: item[1].st_mtime)
    total = sum(st.st_size for _, st in seeds)
    free = free_bytes(archive)
    dropped = []
    for key, st in seeds[:max(0, len(seeds) - KEEP_NEWEST)]:
        if total <= budget and free >= min_free:
            break
        if now - st.st_mtime < GRACE or key in spare:
            continue
        if apply:
            try:
                (archive / (key + SUFFIX)).unlink()
            except OSError:
                continue
        total -= st.st_size
        free += st.st_size
        dropped.append({"key": key, "bytes": st.st_size, "age_hours": round((now - st.st_mtime) / 3600, 1)})
    return dropped


def free_bytes(archive: Path) -> int:
    """Free space for the archive: the image's own, and the X10 Pro's under it."""
    free = shutil.disk_usage(archive).free
    if archive.is_relative_to(MOUNT) and os.path.ismount(HOST_VOLUME):
        free = min(free, shutil.disk_usage(HOST_VOLUME).free)
    return free


def attach() -> str:
    """"" once MOUNT holds the image (attaching it if needed), else why not."""
    if os.path.ismount(MOUNT):
        return ""
    if not IMAGE.is_dir():
        return f"{IMAGE} does not exist (glaeda-seed-archive install --apply creates it)"
    try:
        proc = subprocess.run([HDIUTIL, "attach", "-quiet", "-nobrowse", "-mountpoint", os.fspath(MOUNT),
                               os.fspath(IMAGE)], capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=120)
    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
        return "hdiutil attach timed out"
    return "" if os.path.ismount(MOUNT) else f"hdiutil attach: {proc.stderr.strip()[-160:]}"


def run(apply: bool, archive: Path = ARCHIVE, budget: int = BUDGET, min_free: int = MIN_FREE,
        mounted: bool = False) -> dict:
    """One fill and prune. MOUNTED: ARCHIVE needs no image attached (tests)."""
    record: dict = {"tool": "glaeda-seed-archive", "time": int(time.time()), "apply": apply,
                    "archive": os.fspath(archive)}
    if not mounted and (why := attach()):
        return {**record, "state": "skipped", "reason": why}
    if apply:
        archive.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
    elif not archive.is_dir():
        return {**record, "state": "planned", "reason": "the archive directory does not exist yet"}
    config = pm.lan_config()
    if config is None:
        return {**record, "state": "error", "reason": f"no seeder config at {pm.LAN_CONFIG} "
                "(glaeda-seed-lan install --seeder cmux15 ... cmux-lawrence)"}
    STATE.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    lock = os.open(STATE / "lock", os.O_RDONLY | os.O_CREAT, 0o600)
    try:
        fcntl.flock(lock, fcntl.LOCK_EX | fcntl.LOCK_NB)
    except OSError:
        return {**record, "state": "skipped", "reason": "another run holds the lock"}
    try:
        kept, why = seeder_list(config)
        if why:
            return {**record, "state": "error", "reason": why}
        unreadable: dict[str, str] = {}
        aside: list[str] = []
        have = archived(archive, unreadable, aside)
        record["quarantined_aside"] = len(aside)
        if unreadable:
            record["unreadable"] = quarantine(archive, unreadable, apply)
            for item in record["unreadable"]:
                if item.get("quarantined"):
                    unreadable.pop(item["key"])
        # A seed still sitting unreadable is not fetched over (the rename would hit the same bad entry).
        missing = list(dict.fromkeys(key for key, _ in kept if key not in have and key not in unreadable))
        record["seeder_kept"] = len(kept)
        record["missing"] = len(missing)
        fetched = []
        held = sum(st.st_size for st in have.values())
        if held >= budget or free_bytes(archive) < min_free:
            record["full"] = True  # fetch nothing until prune (of seeds the seeder dropped) makes room
            missing = []
        if apply:
            for key in missing[:MAX_PER_RUN]:
                result = fetch(config, key, archive)
                fetched.append(result)
                if result["outcome"] in ("busy", "unreachable", "refused"):
                    break  # try again next run
        else:
            record["would_fetch"] = missing[:MAX_PER_RUN]
        record["fetched"] = fetched
        record["pruned"] = prune(archive, budget, min_free, apply, {key for key, _ in kept})
        seeds = archived(archive)
        record["archive_seeds"] = len(seeds)
        record["archive_bytes"] = sum(st.st_size for st in seeds.values())
        record["disk_free_bytes"] = free_bytes(archive)
        record["state"] = "applied" if apply else "planned"
        return record
    finally:
        os.close(lock)


def disk_errors(record: dict) -> dict:
    """The run's disk errors (glaeda-disk-errors/v1): entries that read an OSError this run, still unreadable or
    quarantined by it, plus the seeds already sitting aside as .corrupt-* (quarantined_aside, counted from this run's
    listing, so a seed moved aside earlier still says the drive failed). A run that failed whole on an OSError (main)
    counts as one unreadable entry: its reason names the path."""
    unreadable = record.get("unreadable") or []
    keys = {i["key"] for i in unreadable if i.get("key")} | set(record.get("known_unreadable") or [])
    listing = [i["error"] for i in unreadable if not i.get("key") and i.get("error")]
    failed = record.get("state") == "error" and "errno" in str(record.get("reason", ""))
    examples = [f"{i['key']}{SUFFIX}: {i.get('error')}" for i in unreadable if i.get("key")]
    examples += listing + ([record["reason"]] if failed else [])
    return {"schema": DISK_ERRORS_SCHEMA, "service": "seed-archive", "at": int(record.get("time") or time.time()),
            "root": record.get("archive") or os.fspath(ARCHIVE),
            "unreadable": len(keys) + len(listing) + int(failed),
            "still_unreadable": len([i for i in unreadable if i.get("key") and not i.get("quarantined")]),
            "quarantined": int(record.get("quarantined_aside") or 0)
                           + len([i for i in unreadable if i.get("quarantined")]),
            "examples": examples[:DISK_ERRORS_EXAMPLES]}


def write_disk_errors(report: dict) -> None:
    """Replace the disk-errors file with REPORT (atomic). Rewritten when its counts change or every 10 min, so a
    reader can tell a live zero from a stopped job by `at`; a file that cannot be written never fails the run."""
    path = STATE.parent / "disk-errors" / DISK_ERRORS_NAME
    try:
        old = json.loads(path.read_text())
        same = {k: v for k, v in old.items() if k != "at"} == {k: v for k, v in report.items() if k != "at"}
        if same and report["at"] - int(old.get("at") or 0) < 600:
            return
    except (OSError, ValueError, TypeError, AttributeError):
        pass
    try:
        path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        staged = path.with_name(f".{path.name}.{os.getpid()}")
        staged.write_text(json.dumps(report, sort_keys=True) + "\n")
        staged.replace(path)
    except OSError:
        pass


def quiet(record: dict) -> bool:
    """A run that fetched, pruned and reported nothing: not logged, or the log would be one line every 15 s."""
    return (record.get("state") == "applied" and not record.get("missing") and not record.get("fetched")
            and not record.get("unreadable")
            and not record.get("pruned") and not record.get("full"))


def append_log(record: dict) -> None:
    try:
        LOG.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        if LOG.exists() and LOG.stat().st_size > LOG_BYTES:
            LOG.replace(LOG.with_suffix(".jsonl.1"))
        with LOG.open("a") as out:
            out.write(json.dumps(record, sort_keys=True) + "\n")
    except OSError:
        pass


# Keep in step with glaeda-mini-setup LAN_PARENT (this script installs itself without setup).
LAN_PARENT = ["/bin/sh", "-c",
              '"$@" & p=$!; trap "kill -TERM $p 2>/dev/null" TERM HUP INT; s=0; wait $p || s=$?; '
              'while kill -0 $p 2>/dev/null; do wait $p; s=$?; done; exit $s', "glaeda-lan"]


def plist(program: Path) -> dict:
    return {
        "Label": LABEL,
        # A system daemon runs as the user that owns the archive and its keys, with that user's HOME.
        "UserName": pwd.getpwuid(os.getuid()).pw_name,
        # /bin/sh as the job's process, /usr/bin/python3 under it: Local Network Privacy then lets its
        # /usr/bin/ssh reach the LAN on macOS 27 too (glaeda-mini-setup LAN_PARENT, the same wrapper).
        "ProgramArguments": [*LAN_PARENT, "/usr/bin/python3", "-I", os.fspath(program), "--apply"],
        "StartInterval": INTERVAL,
        "RunAtLoad": True,
        # hdiutil attach leaves diskimages-helper serving the mount. launchd ends what a finished job left in its
        # process group unless told not to, which would pull the image from under the volume every 15 s run.
        "AbandonProcessGroup": True,
        "EnvironmentVariables": {"PATH": "/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin", "HOME": os.fspath(HOME)},
        # Every run prints its record; LOG (bounded) keeps the ones that did something.
        "StandardOutPath": "/dev/null",
        "StandardErrorPath": os.fspath(HOME / "Library/Logs/glaeda-seed-archive.err"),
    }


def root(*argv: str) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:
    prefix = [] if os.geteuid() == 0 else SUDO_PREFIX
    return subprocess.run([*prefix, *argv], capture_output=True, text=True)


def have_root() -> bool:
    return os.geteuid() == 0 or root("true").returncode == 0


def retire_agent() -> bool:
    """Boot out the old gui/UID LaunchAgent and remove its plist; True if there was one."""
    old = HOME / "Library/LaunchAgents" / f"{LABEL}.plist"
    loaded = subprocess.run([LAUNCHCTL, "print", f"gui/{os.getuid()}/{LABEL}"], capture_output=True).returncode == 0
    subprocess.run([LAUNCHCTL, "bootout", f"gui/{os.getuid()}/{LABEL}"], capture_output=True)
    existed = old.exists()
    old.unlink(missing_ok=True)
    return existed or loaded


def daemon_loaded() -> bool:
    return subprocess.run([LAUNCHCTL, "print", f"system/{LABEL}"], capture_output=True).returncode == 0


def install_daemon(report: dict, want: bytes) -> None:
    path = DAEMON_DIR / f"{LABEL}.plist"
    current = path.read_bytes() if path.exists() else b""
    if current == want and daemon_loaded():
        report["retired_agent"] = retire_agent()
        report["loaded"], report["daemon"] = True, "current"
        return
    if not have_root():
        if daemon_loaded():
            report["retired_agent"] = retire_agent()
            report["loaded"], report["daemon"] = True, "adopted"
            report["warning"] = "the loaded LaunchDaemon differs and there is no passwordless sudo to replace it"
            return
        staged = STATE.parent / f"{LABEL}.plist"
        staged.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
        staged.write_bytes(want)
        report["loaded"] = False
        report["error"] = (f"no passwordless sudo; as root: install -m 644 {staged} {path} && chown root:wheel {path} "
                           f"&& launchctl bootstrap system {path} (from a controller: fleet-sudo HOST ...)")
        return
    report["retired_agent"] = retire_agent()
    staged = STATE.parent / f"{LABEL}.plist.{os.getpid()}"
    staged.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    staged.write_bytes(want)
    try:
        root(LAUNCHCTL, "bootout", f"system/{LABEL}")
        for step in (("install", "-m", "0644", os.fspath(staged), os.fspath(path)),
                     ("chown", "root:wheel", os.fspath(path))):
            done = root(*step)
            if done.returncode:
                report["loaded"], report["error"] = False, done.stderr.strip()[-200:]
                return
        boot = root(LAUNCHCTL, "bootstrap", "system", os.fspath(path))
        report["loaded"], report["daemon"] = boot.returncode == 0, "installed"
        if boot.returncode:
            report["error"] = boot.stderr.strip()[-200:]
    finally:
        staged.unlink(missing_ok=True)


def install(apply: bool) -> dict:
    program = SCRIPT_DIR / "glaeda-seed-archive"
    path = DAEMON_DIR / f"{LABEL}.plist"
    want = plistlib.dumps(plist(program))
    current = path.read_bytes() if path.exists() else b""
    report = {"tool": "glaeda-seed-archive", "mode": "install", "apply": apply, "plist": os.fspath(path),
              "state": "current" if current == want else ("stale" if current else "missing"),
              "image": "present" if IMAGE.is_dir() else "missing", "mounted": os.path.ismount(MOUNT)}
    if apply and not IMAGE.is_dir():
        if not os.path.ismount(HOST_VOLUME):
            return {**report, "error": f"{HOST_VOLUME} is not mounted"}
        subprocess.run([HDIUTIL, "create", "-quiet", "-type", "SPARSEBUNDLE", "-fs", "APFS", "-size", IMAGE_SIZE,
                        "-volname", MOUNT.name, os.fspath(IMAGE)], check=True, timeout=300)
        report["image"] = "created"
    if apply:
        if why := attach():
            return {**report, "error": why}
        ARCHIVE.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
        moved = 0
        if OLD_ARCHIVE.is_dir():
            for old in OLD_ARCHIVE.iterdir():
                if old.name.endswith(SUFFIX) and pm.KEY_RE.fullmatch(old.name[:-len(SUFFIX)]):
                    shutil.move(os.fspath(old), os.fspath(ARCHIVE / old.name))
                    moved += 1
                elif ".incoming-" in old.name or old.name.startswith("._"):
                    old.unlink()
            try:
                OLD_ARCHIVE.rmdir()
            except OSError as error:
                report["old_archive"] = f"left in place: {error}"
        report["moved"] = moved
        install_daemon(report, want)
    return report


def uninstall(apply: bool) -> dict:
    """Remove both the daemon and any old agent; the archive and its image stay."""
    path = DAEMON_DIR / f"{LABEL}.plist"
    report = {"tool": "glaeda-seed-archive", "mode": "uninstall", "apply": apply, "plist": os.fspath(path),
              "daemon": "present" if path.exists() else "absent",
              "agent": "present" if (HOME / "Library/LaunchAgents" / f"{LABEL}.plist").exists() else "absent"}
    if not apply:
        return report
    retire_agent()
    report["agent"] = "removed"
    if path.exists():
        if not have_root():
            report["error"] = f"ROOT STEP NEEDED: sudo launchctl bootout system/{LABEL}; sudo rm {path}"
            return report
        root(LAUNCHCTL, "bootout", f"system/{LABEL}")
        root("rm", "-f", os.fspath(path))
        report["daemon"] = "removed"
    return report


def main(argv: list[str]) -> int:
    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__.splitlines()[0])
    parser.add_argument("command", nargs="?", choices=("install", "uninstall"))
    parser.add_argument("--apply", action="store_true")
    args = parser.parse_args(argv)
    if args.command == "uninstall":
        report = uninstall(args.apply)
        print(json.dumps(report))
        return 1 if report.get("error") else 0
    if args.command == "install":
        report = install(args.apply)
        print(json.dumps(report))
        return 1 if report.get("error") or (args.apply and not report.get("loaded")) else 0
    try:
        record = run(args.apply)
    except OSError as error:  # EIO from the volume or image anywhere else in a run: reported, not a traceback
        record = {"tool": "glaeda-seed-archive", "time": int(time.time()), "apply": args.apply, "state": "error",
                  "reason": f"{type(error).__name__} errno {error.errno}: {error.strerror} ({error.filename})"}
    if args.apply and not quiet(record):
        append_log(record)
    # Only a run that listed the archive (or failed on an OSError) says anything about the disk: a skipped run (no
    # image, the lock) or a seeder error before the listing must not clear a count with a zero.
    if args.apply and ("quarantined_aside" in record or "errno" in str(record.get("reason", ""))):
        write_disk_errors(disk_errors(record))
    print(json.dumps(record))
    return 1 if record["state"] == "error" else 0


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
